A||||15||fiero56||neighbor thinks stock exhaust is too loud?||||1||
Z||000000||fiero56||07-09-2001||10:30 PM||||I just moved to a new apartment a couple of months ago, and very recently began driving my "beast" '86SE 2.8 4-speed daily in place of my quiet mellow Formula.<P>As I pulled in around 10pm tonight, I see an older guy(early 40s?) a few apartments down jump off his couch, and bolt out the door, to stand on his porch. As I'm getting out he appears to be in "confrontation mode", but I had my ratty jeans on, and a torn t-shirt(its laundry day, they were all that was clean), and he takes a step back as I say "hi." Must have caught him off guard, becuase he stammered, then backed into his apartment and closed the door. <P>I've got stock exhaust on the car, no leaks, only 105K miles. It is pretty loud though. I bet I hear from either the guy or leasing office about my exhaust. I'll have to wait and see. I can't wait to rev 'er up in the morning out front at 7am. I'm grinning, I hope his window is open <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I'll just say it is factory, and if GM passed it out the door, its perfectly legal.<P>Hmmm, maybe I should go for a drive later tonight...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Santa Cruzer||07-09-2001||10:42 PM||||yeah man mines the same but i love it gives it that power feel! i also have an 86 se automatic though!! keep em stock!!!<P>------------------<BR>red candy apple copper burgandy color,tan interior all options,american racing rims,Pioneer Cd Player,pioneer 120w speakers"in factory location",sony ****  amp,and workin' on a girl to go with the package<BR>www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/dts.html  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/me!!!.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroburton||07-09-2001||11:49 PM||||bust his ear drums with your stock .||||reg||6
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||07-09-2001||11:57 PM||||Hey 56!<BR>Bet ya got a plug missing from your cat converter...<BR>Seems they rust out and blow out...<BR>I have fixed 2 cats with that problem...<BR>But if you enjoy anoying the neibor, skip it!!!<BR>Course, its not as fun as the feud I had a few years ago, open headers and slicks down the neibors drive at 3 am ended it...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||07-10-2001||12:44 AM||||I used to live In Hilliard Ohio, just west of columbus and on the final approach path for Port Columbus Airport. This neighbor was always complaining about noise, whether is was working on cars in the garage or mowing the lawn. On one particular nite, I was flying back from a Nascar race at about 2 am. I had a Cherokee Lance at the time. ITs a very big 6 passenger, single engine, 3 blade prop plane. I had this brilliant idea when Columbus approach control put me on the west approach to land. I knew this went over my house so I let the plane drop with the engine at idle till i was a minimum altitude over the house then poured full power on till I climbed back up 1,000 ft. When I got home there was stuff that had fell off my walls laying all thru the house on the carpet. LOL. Ya know she never complained any more after that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierohoho||07-10-2001||01:27 AM||||My advise would be to leave well enough alone. <BR>Don't provoke the guy. Remember, you can't watch your Fieros all the time. <P>This guy may do one of three things: <P>#1 Resort to vandalism on one or both of your cars. You could be gone and he would have free run on the other car. <P>#2 He could raise heck with management, if you like moving go for it. <P>#3 He could complain to the cops, he should by now know your schedule and he could tell them, next thing you know a bored cop sits waiting for you to come home, bang, fixit ticket. <P>He could make your life just as miserable as you could make his, best bet and cheapest, coast into your spot until you check the exhaust like Fierowrecker said. <P>Sorry about the lecture, it happens as you get older, you'll see.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000006||pontiacs4me||07-10-2001||01:36 AM||||he would probably love my other car.  I have a 1973 firebird formula, headers 3" dual exhaust routed though 2 chamber flowmasters then ground dumps in front of the rear end.  It shakes windows 200 feet away.  But its all legal.  Ive driven the car for 3 years and 44k like this, and never been pulled over for loud exhaust.  If the guy complains tell him to kiss you ass, if he damages your car or cars, find out what he drives and see if it is fireproof.||||reg||1
Z||000007||The Fieromaster||07-10-2001||01:38 AM||||Up here in ashtabula county Ohio we dont need cat's cause we have no emissions tests.. Do what i did once... back the car up the driveway and bounce her off the red zone area a few times at like 2am... hehehee!  Yea im too loud now huh... hehehe!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">     <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||10
Z||000008||lowCG||07-10-2001||02:28 AM||||I'd just try to mind my own business,and definately don't get defensive but know that whoever it is that you may see in court,or manager's office will need to have some sort of certified form of decibel reading before any judgement is made against you and your car.<BR>Otherwise it's just plain hearsay and harassement directed at you.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haze_Performance||07-10-2001||03:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>I just moved to a new apartment a couple of months ago, and very recently began driving my "beast" '86SE 2.8 4-speed daily in place of my quiet mellow Formula.<P>As I pulled in around 10pm tonight, I see an older guy(early 40s?) a few apartments down jump off his couch, and bolt out the door, to stand on his porch. As I'm getting out he appears to be in "confrontation mode", but I had my ratty jeans on, and a torn t-shirt(its laundry day, they were all that was clean), and he takes a step back as I say "hi." Must have caught him off guard, becuase he stammered, then backed into his apartment and closed the door. <P>I've got stock exhaust on the car, no leaks, only 105K miles. It is pretty loud though. I bet I hear from either the guy or leasing office about my exhaust. I'll have to wait and see. I can't wait to rev 'er up in the morning out front at 7am. I'm grinning, I hope his window is open  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I'll just say it is factory, and if GM passed it out the door, its perfectly legal.<P>Hmmm, maybe I should go for a drive later tonight...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I> That's funny. I live in a snooty suburb apartment complex, I threw a pair of dumps (cutoff exhaust) on my Mustang. I came home at around 8:30pm and as I drove to my apartment, I had just about EVERY person standing outside shaking there heads. I only kept them on for 2 days but some of the neighbors still give me dirty looks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR></I></B></FONT><P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/classicfieroowners3.gif">   </A><BR><I><B>Click above to visit my website.</B></I>||||reg||14
