Z||000011||stsmithgt||07-10-2001||10:04 AM||||Well, if you make it to the point of not getting kicked out and the ol' fart can't do much about it, try cruising into the parking lot with your exhaust at a resonant frequency so it sounds twice as loud!  At around 2600 RPM I can get the sound of my exhuast to reverberate(sp?) off the buildings pretty good. I have a new cat and muffler and can still set off plenty car alarms doing that. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Of course, I have no problem with my neighbors so I keep it pretty quiet there. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||The Fieromaster||07-10-2001||12:02 PM||||Yea HAZE your the man!! hehehe!  I thought my 6 cylenders bounced off the building walls really well hehe!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">     <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000013||Raydar||07-10-2001||01:15 PM||||When I had my T-top Formula, I put an IRM "dual resonator only" system on my car. Left the cat in place. I *hated* driving out of my neighborhood at 7:00 AM.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>That sucker would resonate at about 2500 RPM and make your eyeballs vibrate. <BR>I could set off just about every car alarm in the parking deck at work.<BR>Ended up having a bullet glasspack welded in between the cat and the "Y". Was STILL loud, but at least you could carry on a conversation in the car. <BR>I really think the stock system sounds better. Just wish it was a bit louder.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ken Wittlief||07-10-2001||01:21 PM||||personally I find that most cars that sound like harleys with straight pipes are dissapointing to drive<P>  Ive yet to see one that delivers the kinda HP that it SOUNDS like it should have - and after driving around for a half hour or so it just sounds trashy - like the garbage truck is coming down the street.<P> I like machines that are powerful and silent - feels like some incredible magnetic force is pulling you forwards - if you ever cracked open the throttle on one of the original Honda Goldwings in second gear then you'll know what Im talking about.<P>  But then again, I like sailboats too. My hobie 16 can go from 0 to 25 in about 3 seconds - dead silent - and you better be holding onto something when I pull the mainsail in.||||reg||1
Z||000015||fiero56||07-10-2001||05:41 PM||||There isn't a whole lot to vandalize on my SE. Its stock, with bad paint. He could beat on it if he felt like it, but I find his '00 G/A with the damn double-horn-honk-when-you-lock-the-doors to be most annoying. He was gone this morning, and isn't back yet. My neighbor has an SE-R with aftermarket exhaust, and a few "extras" under the hood, that thing isn't a whole lot quieter than my Fiero. I won't provoke him, I doubt there is much he can do. Cops can do a sound check if they want, but I'm pretty sure its within legal specs.<P>I tried to be friendly with him, he's the one who backed into the house and quietly closed his door, as if realizing for some reason he made a mistake. I'm not sweating it, I'll be laughing if I get a notice about my exhaust though.||||reg||1
